     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Programs and languages",
     "md": "A **program** is a set of instructions that a computer follows. We write programs in a **programming language**. Computers only run **machine code** (binary), so a **translator** (compiler or interpreter) turns our language into machine code."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Variables and types",
     "md": "A **variable** is a named box that stores a value, e.g. age = 14. Types: **integer** (whole numbers), **real** (decimals), **string** (text) and **Boolean** (TRUE/FALSE). A **constant** never changes."
    },
